@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - One real run (SPY chain snapshot through MCP, measured 2026-08-30)

actor "Agent" as A
participant "MCP server\n(stdio, JSON-RPC)" as M
participant "CLI command\nchain.run(args)" as C
participant "Provider\n(registry pick)" as P
participant "Engine\n(via engine_bridge)" as E
database "Disk\n~/TradingDesk/option-desk" as D

A -> M : tools/call option_chain_snapshot {symbol: SPY}
M -> C : chain.run(args)
C -> P : resolve(option_chain), then fetch
P --> C : 607 contracts, spot, listed expiries
C -> E : implied_vol per contract
E --> C : 595 solved, 12 refused as unidentified
note right of E
The refusals are the feature:
a contract whose price carries no
volatility information gets iv: null,
counted in counts.without_iv.
A guessed volatility would produce a
complete, fictional Greek ladder that
looks exactly as authoritative as a real one.
end note
C -> C : validate against chain_snapshot schema
C -> D : atomic write, tmp then replace\n(previous file archived first)
C --> M : {artifact, contracts, with_iv, degraded, notes}
M --> A : JSON summary

note over A, D
degraded and notes are different fields. Degraded: the output is lower quality than
the pipeline can produce (provider fell back, rate not fetched, engine absent).
Notes: ordinary observations. Collapsing them would make every artifact degraded
and the flag worthless.
end note

caption Reproducible from shell/tests/test_mcp_server.py, which drives every tool over a real stdio session.
@enduml
